  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="unit_runlet_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>runlet, a cask or vessel of varying capacity; the quantity of liquor contained in this (large runlets appear usually to have varied between 12 and 18½ gallons, small ones between a pint or quart and 3 or 4 gallons) (OED s.v. runlet1) | as a packing unit for dry goods of no particular size | as a packing unit for wine | as a measure of granum | cask, a transport unit for liquid goods | meaning unknown</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
